      "content": "#include \"knn.h\"\n#include <limits.h>\n\n#define KNN_PARALLEL_HISTOGRAM_THRESHOLD 8192\n\nchar knn(int n_groups, Group * groups, int k, Point to_evaluate) {\n    char * labels = (char *) malloc(sizeof(char) * k);\n    float * distances = (float *) malloc(sizeof(float) * k);\n\n    int i, j, x, y;\n\n    for (i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n        labels[i] = -1;\n        distances[i] = -1;\n    }\n\n    for (i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        Group g = groups[i];\n\n        for (j = 0; j < g.length; j++) {\n            float d = euclidean_distance_no_sqrt(to_evaluate, g.points[j]);\n\n            for (x = 0; x < k; x++) {\n                if (d < distances[x] || distances[x] == -1) {\n                    for (y = k - 1; y > x; y--) {\n                        distances[y] = distances[y - 1];\n                        labels[y] = labels[y - 1];\n                    }\n\n                    distances[x] = d;\n                    labels[x] = g.label;\n\n                    break;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (k >= KNN_PARALLEL_HISTOGRAM_THRESHOLD) {\n        int frequencies[UCHAR_MAX + 1] = {0};\n\n        #pragma omp parallel for schedule(static) reduction(+:frequencies[:UCHAR_MAX + 1])\n        for (i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n            frequencies[(unsigned char) labels[i]]++;\n        }\n\n        char most_frequent = labels[0];\n        int most_frequent_count = 0;\n\n        for (int value = CHAR_MIN; value <= CHAR_MAX; value++) {\n            int frequency = frequencies[(unsigned char) (char) value];\n            if (frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = (char) value;\n                most_frequent_count = frequency;\n            }\n        }\n\n        return most_frequent;\n    }\n\n    qsort(labels, k, sizeof(char), compare_for_sort);\n\n    char most_frequent = labels[0];\n    int most_frequent_count = 1;\n    int current_frequency = 1;\n\n    for (i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n        if (labels[i] != labels[i - 1]) {\n            if (current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n                most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n                most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n            }\n\n            current_frequency = 1;\n        } else {\n            current_frequency++;\n        }\n\n        if (i == k - 1 && current_frequency > most_frequent_count) {\n            most_frequent = labels[i - 1];\n            most_frequent_count = current_frequency;\n        }\n    }\n\n    return most_frequent;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n_groups = parse_number_of_groups();\n    \n    Group * groups = (Group *) malloc(sizeof(Group) * n_groups);\n\n    for (int i = 0; i < n_groups; i++) {\n        groups[i] = parse_next_group();\n    }\n\n    int k = parse_k();\n\n    Point to_evaluate = parse_point();\n\n    printf(\"%c\", knn(n_groups, groups, k, to_evaluate));\n}\n",
      "path": "src/knn.c"
    }
  ],
  "hypothesis": "For large k, counting the selected labels in a parallel static-scheduled histogram should be cheaper than sorting them, while a threshold keeps OpenMP startup overhead out of small-k cases. Scanning bins in plain-char order with strict-greater updates should preserve the existing plurality tie rule, including sentinel labels.",
  "notes": "This is an unmeasured candidate. The histogram and reduction storage are local and initialized on each call. Correctness and speed remain for the controller to evaluate.",
  "sources_kept": [],
  "transformations": [
    "Keep the existing top-k selection and qsort path for k below a generic granularity threshold.",
    "For large k, use an OpenMP static parallel-for with an array-section sum reduction to build a 256-value label histogram.",
    "Select the plurality by scanning values from CHAR_MIN through CHAR_MAX and updating only for a strictly larger count, preserving the qsort path's signed-char ordering and first-label tie behavior."
